Subject: ath11k: further reduce TX completion and monitor pools for AX53

Experimental build-wide limits for this experimental 256 MiB AX53 build.
Must follow 953-ath11k-reduce-rx-rings-experimental-256m.patch.

Small-buffer prior art: Ziyang Huang's OpenWrt PR #21495 reduces TX
completion entries to 2048 and monitor destination entries to 128:
https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/21495
Use less aggressive 8192/512 entries here; also shrink the separately
allocated monitor link-descriptor pool from 4096 to 1024 entries.

DP_TX_IDR_SIZE and ATH11K_TX_COMPL_NEXT derive from DP_TX_COMP_RING_SIZE,
as do the hardware completion ring and software tx_status allocation.
Keep their capacities and wrap arithmetic consistent. Do not shrink
DP_RXDMA_REFILL_RING_SIZE: it is passed as the RX filter buffer size in
monitor configuration, not allocated as another refill queue here.

This is not an upstream-validated configuration. Smaller pools can lose
completion/monitor events or limit burst throughput. Long-term throughput and
stability validation remain pending; retain patch 953 alone
as the previously exercised fallback.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp.h
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@
 #define DP_WBM_RELEASE_RING_SIZE	64
 #define DP_TCL_DATA_RING_SIZE		512
 #define DP_TCL_DATA_RING_SIZE_WCN6750	2048
-#define DP_TX_COMP_RING_SIZE		32768
+#define DP_TX_COMP_RING_SIZE		8192
 #define DP_TX_IDR_SIZE			DP_TX_COMP_RING_SIZE
 #define DP_TCL_CMD_RING_SIZE		32
 #define DP_TCL_STATUS_RING_SIZE		32
@@ -221,8 +221,8 @@
 #define DP_RXDMA_ERR_DST_RING_SIZE	1024
 #define DP_RXDMA_MON_STATUS_RING_SIZE	128
 #define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_BUF_RING_SIZE	128
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	2048
-#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	4096
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DST_RING_SIZE	512
+#define DP_RXDMA_MONITOR_DESC_RING_SIZE	1024
 
 #define DP_RX_RELEASE_RING_NUM	3
